  "_comment": "Special enemy catalogue. An arena enables types through its 'special_enemies' setting (see /zombies settings > Special enemies). entity: candidate entity types, the first one the server knows is used (ZOMBIE is the final fallback). health: base + per_round * (round - 1), or zombie_multiplier x the round's zombie health when set; per_extra_player scales it for co-op. speed and scale multiply the mob's own values (scale needs 1.20.5+). model: pack item model worn on the head when the resource pack is on. sounds: event -> sounds.json key, default special.<id>.<event> (spawn, ambient, attack, death, explode, round). points replace the normal kill points. reward_powerup drops when a player kills it, round_end_powerup when a dedicated round of this type is cleared. round_count: how many spawn in a dedicated round (base + per_player per extra player). lifetime_seconds: despawn (escape) after this long, 0 = never. behaviour: steal_perk | steal_weapon | boss | napalm | shrieker; options tune it (boss attack steal_perk: flee_after_steal makes it run off with one perk for flee_seconds; grab_teleport throws the player to a spot players have stood on, at least teleport_min_distance away). default_rule is what the settings menu adds when the type is switched on.",
